fields.comment:
// The ingress lock protects lifecycle admission and public configuration;
// child completion fields use that same gate (see ChildSubmission). Turn
// scheduling fields below are touched exclusively by the actor task.

// Configuration seeds the policy; this field alone owns runtime updates.
// The actor captures it once per turn, so a settings change cannot move an
// in-flight turn's boundary. Negative constructor seeds retain Chapter 5's
// library-only unlimited behavior; the runtime setter accepts >= 0 only.

// Ensemble owns every Agent. A delegated Agent also belongs to one Agent
// parent, which owns its lifetime. Local IDs address siblings, not the root
// application's standalone name index. Neither relationship is a service copy.

// This is only the last emitted projection for duplicate suppression.
// Open status derives current activity from actor state. Once admission
// closes, readers use this final/closing projection without racing that state.

// The contract is immutable and value-like. Publication and generation fields
// are protected by ingress, including during disk replacement. The Agent's
// explicit home owns the artifact path independently of History save paths.

// Set only during construction through Sandbox. History's save path may be
// anywhere permitted by that Sandbox, including a session subdirectory; it
// never supplies or changes this distinct data-home fact.

comments:
/// <summary>A pending reply is an edge strongly owned by its asking and receiving
/// Agents, not a value. For a human question both owners are the root Agent: that
/// root is the host's inbox, not a fabricated Agent representing the person.
/// Answering or destruction removes both links; it never destroys either Agent.</summary>

/// <summary>Value-like observation of ownership, not a second owner or registry.
/// Agent is the actual identity, as in AgentObservation; the snapshot grants no
/// task-control authority and does not keep that Agent logically alive. Names
/// and child IDs remain on Agent. Two branches may have the same local child ID.
/// Children captures membership, not live scheduling or submission state.</summary>

// Value-like immutable protocol snapshot, not a service or another credential
// authority. Credentials owns its lifetime. The old registration is retained
// only to detect intervening writes (including another process's logout). No
// generated ToString may disclose the verifier or saved account tokens.

/// <summary>
/// The deliberately narrow OIDC wire vocabulary. Auth owns its implementations;
/// callers supply trusted issuer keys, never key URLs taken from an untrusted JWT.
/// No credentials or validation state are retained here.
/// </summary>

// Value-like private storage vocabulary, not model conversation. Keep these
// records internal and never serialize them with the History/event codecs.
// A class rather than a record avoids a generated ToString that prints secrets.

// Value-like diagnostic records, not conversation state. Capture owns fresh byte
// arrays; callers may inspect or edit their returned copy without changing Engine. Bytes measure a local
// approximation of provider prompt order; they are never token/billing counts.

/// <summary>Value-like join progress. A non-null Submissions dictionary is the
/// final result (possibly empty). Otherwise Questions contains newly observed
/// questions, not consumed replies. Typed payloads retain their JSON values.</summary>

/// <summary>Value-like finalized output. Cursor is this child's durable History
/// sequence, not a byte offset or global identity. Status is a separate current
/// actor snapshot; idle does not imply submission.</summary>

/// <summary>Ensemble-owned read-only source of Codex's file-backed ChatGPT grant.
/// Construction selects a path, never discovers profiles or reads credentials.
/// Every send reads a fresh pair; Codex alone signs in, rotates and revokes it.</summary>

/// <summary>Value-like parent-authored selection identity. Null Source means
/// conversation; file sources graduate one band. IDs grant no filesystem access.
/// SelectionHash binds the exact selected source and destination bytes in the
/// staged disk record to this launch. Replay never reads those files.</summary>

/// <summary>Immutable request settings. The Agent publishes the current value;
/// each send freezes it before transport. Configured projections reference the
/// credential owner rather than copying its secrets. Credentials are not logged.</summary>

fields.comment:
// Explicit selected-model policy, not guessed from a provider/name prefix.
// Off by default: ordinary configurations retain whole results until the
// byte ladder or an explicit clearing operation selects them.

// Launch policy narrows recorded grants without editing historical manuals.
// Safe mode removes shell access, not file access. Web permission controls
// the named web-search skill; it is not a general network firewall.

// Value-like host policy for confined processes only. Null means inherit;
// an explicit empty list drops external reads. Native file tools stay rooted.
// Sandbox resolves existing physical targets before admitting any process.

comments:
/// <summary>Value-like, immutable selected conversation source. It owns no Agent
/// or file relationships. Exact entries (including their sequence/part identities)
/// are retained for later stale-result validation; readable text is derived only
/// when preparing compressor input. Selection alone never removes source.</summary>

/// <summary>Optional Ensemble-owned protected credential storage shared by its
/// Agents. Construction registers both ends but performs no file or network I/O.
/// Supply a dedicated private directory, not a conversation workspace.</summary>

// An owned diagnostic file resource, not another logger identity or service bag.
// Callers transfer a seekable file on successful construction and close this
// writer only after their work joins. Borrowed diagnostic writers are not wrapped.

fields.comment:
// A separate strong child: Codex owns its grant, while our public OAuth
// Credentials child owns a different registration and renewal protocol.
// The existing credentialsGate protects both optional relationships.

// Question edges span two Agents. One graph lock makes both relationships
// atomic without acquiring parent/child ingress locks in opposite orders.
// Code holding this lock must never enter an Agent's ingress lock.

// The application container, not any one actor's personal home. It holds
// ensemble.json and agents/<name>/ for sibling top-level actors. A library
// instance may omit storage when it only hosts transient Agents.

// Display identity is independent of provider call IDs and opaque payloads.
// ResponseID is the durable RequestSent sequence; IDs are parser-local,
// including zero. Empty metadata means a historical/non-response event.

comments:
/// <summary>Application-owned global settings file, explicitly supplied by the
/// host. Agent policy remains in each Agent's settings.json. Reads never create
/// files; writes preserve unrelated fields and never retarget an Agent.</summary>

/// <summary>Immutable value-like patch. Null leaves a setting unchanged; an
/// empty file clears configuration. IdleSeconds is validated legacy data, not an active delay.
/// Ordinary registered children persist these settings for restart; standalone Agents remain session-local.</summary>

// A replaceable I/O boundary, not a copied Agent service. One message is one
// JSON-RPC envelope. The client owns its transport and closes it on destruction.
// Closing must release a blocked receive; sends may overlap at the caller.

// Each Job owns its process, cancellation and output stream. Bytes on disk are
// authoritative; notifications contain no output. A single cursor records what
// observers have already received, independent of canonical conversation events.

fields.comment:
// Remote completion is ordered structured content, not a process byte stream.
// The first terminal observation advances the cursor past this value. Retain
// it until destruction so automatic collection can read it independently;
// later ordinary observations still return only unseen byte output.

comments:
// Value-like recorded report. It cannot restart a process during replay.
// Origin identifies the admitted call within its owning Agent, not a later
// wait/input call. Empty origins in historical records remain unknown.

// A host's one connected browser target. Mcp owns the registration; after a
// skill claims it, both this registration and the ordinary manager/skill own
// the client. Disconnect cascades to that client, never to the Agent or skill.
//
// A registration serves one protocol session. Closing a skill closes its I/O;
// a fresh connection requires a fresh registration, not reuse of old RPC IDs.

// Concrete owned HTTP boundary. Each POST has its own lifetime; the receive
// queue joins replies back to the existing client's numeric request identities.
// No GET stream, event resumption, redirects, cookies or automatic retry.

/// <summary>Agent-owned corpus and transaction I/O. History remains the authority
/// for acceptance; this child never appends events or starts model work. All paths
/// follow Parent → Sandbox and Parent → DataDirectory, not copied services.</summary>

/// <summary>Value-like byte policy. Zero sizes select defaults, not token limits.
/// Disabling hides this band without deleting files. Graduation thresholds are
/// derived from this single size: trigger above twice budget, reduce toward budget.</summary>

/// <summary>Value-like exact captured input. Conversation uses the existing
/// Context codec to retain part identities, not just readable text. File entries
/// retain exact UTF-8 text; destination null means absence, not an empty file.
/// The worker may read this immutable value but has no disk authority from it.</summary>

/// <summary>Immutable value-like memory data, not a grant or an owning relationship.
/// ID is stable within its band; it is never a path or permission to open a file.
/// Timestamp orders entries oldest-first; exact text survives replay and save.</summary>

/// <summary>Immutable per-Agent memory policy, independent of the existing
/// context-capacity setting. Conversation defaults to 3,000 bytes;
/// corpus bands default to 1,500. Graduation thresholds are always twice budget
/// and budget. SOUL never graduates and MEMORY is terminal.</summary>

/// <summary>Value-like outcome of one joined compressor attempt. Usage belongs
/// to this attempt even on failure; only a nonblank Summary can become a staged
/// candidate. This value never confers filesystem or History authority.</summary>

/// <summary>Value-like, coherent view of one Engine's current-process usage.
/// Latest is absent before the first completed response. Rows retain the actual
/// model/tier under which counts accrued; totals are derived from those rows.
/// Neither dollar amounts nor restored History seed the meter.</summary>

/// <summary>A configured offering, strongly owned by one endpoint. Name is the
/// provider-facing model name; ID is its stable local configuration identity.
/// Two endpoints may offer the same Name without sharing identity or funding.</summary>

/// <summary>Explicit authentication/funding choice, strongly owned by Ensemble.
/// It owns an API key only in API-key mode. OAuth/Codex stores remain independent
/// owners with weak, bidirectional bindings. No token is copied into a Model.
/// Losing a source invalidates the binding; it never changes its Kind.</summary>

/// <summary>A configured service and wire surface, strongly owned by its vendor.
/// It owns configured model offerings, not requests or credential renewal work.
/// This graph alone grants no transport access.</summary>

// Value-like renderer capabilities and Ensemble policy, not live discovery or
// a claim that an account can access the model.
// Default arrays mean no verified reasoning options. Exact rows avoid prefix guesses.

/// <summary>Documentary choice information, never permission to send. Availability
/// checks local relationships and request policy, not remote account entitlement
/// or server health. No endpoint address or credential is exposed here.</summary>

/// <summary>A configured vendor, strongly owned by Ensemble. This identity is
/// independent of the historical Vendor enum used by wire codecs: an Ollama
/// endpoint may speak Chat Completions without becoming the OpenAI vendor.</summary>

// A value, not a device or service owner. Only validated, canonical browser WAV
// bytes can construct it. Duration is derived from those bytes, never supplied
// by a browser clock or an untrusted container-duration field.

/// <summary>Immutable replay receipt, not a live worker. Removal is held without
/// changing active source. Committed retains the replacement for crash recovery
/// until a terminal outcome confirms disk finalization.</summary>

/// <summary>Value-like snapshot and journal policy. Audit keeps the same journal
/// untruncated on disk; it never enlarges working History in memory. Default
/// retention keeps the preceding handoff window and the validated backup suffix.
/// A null Agent policy opts out of lifecycle persistence; explicit Save alone
/// does not activate a journal.</summary>

/// <summary>An expected, token-free refusal at the plan-credential boundary.
/// It remains an InvalidOperationException for direct Engine callers. The actor
/// recognizes this type, not arbitrary implementation exceptions, for narration.</summary>

/// <summary>Agent-owned local search indexes. Construction does no disk work.
/// History and Memory still own replay and recovery; this object only reads
/// eligible corpus bytes and caches derived, immutable search statistics.</summary>

/// <summary>Value-like retrieved data, distinct from the user's words. The
/// immutable attachment owns its recorded bytes and complete-source hashes;
/// removing this part from retained context removes its suppression identities.</summary>

/// <summary>Agent-owned filesystem boundary. An empty launch root retains full
/// access. A confined owner retains a directory handle, not just a path prefix.
/// Streams returned by OpenFile belong to callers, which must dispose them.
/// Process confinement is a separate operation, not implied by Resolve.</summary>

// Value-like immutable submission contract. It has no owning Agent and no
// mutable validation cache: children can retain it without lifetime machinery.
// A null schema selects legacy text normalization; an explicit schema never does.

// Value-like exact decimal number used only during schema admission/validation.
// JSON numbers are finite decimals, so rational arithmetic needs no rounding,
// guessed epsilon, or floating-point conversion. Literal/exponent limits bound
// BigInteger sizes before this representation is constructed.

// A bounded compatibility subset, not a general JSON Schema validator. Only
// unconditional properties/items paths and explicit pattern+maxLength strings
// are adapted. Tool keeps the sole authoritative schema; projection is a copy.

// Value-like keys and measurements, never parents or mutable pricing accounts.
// Model/tier are reported by the response. Empty model or absent tier means
// unknown identity, not permission to guess from the selected routing alias.

/// <summary>Optional, separately funded OpenAI API-key transcription owner.
/// Never consults an Agent's provider, plan selection, environment or credentials.
/// One request at a time; no automatic retry, persistence, tracing or chat send.</summary>
